---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import FAQList from '../components/FAQList.astro';
import { images } from '../data/assets';
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'Custom Group Trip Planning',href:'/custom-group-trip-planning/'}];
const faqs=[
 {q:'How custom can the itinerary be?',a:'The planning can begin from the group and trip objective rather than a fixed package. The final degree of customization depends on supplier availability, destination rules, schedule, budget, and group size.'},
 {q:'Can you start from a trip another company already quoted?',a:'Yes. We can review the objectives and structure you are considering, but we build our own recommendations and supplier approach rather than copying another provider’s protected itinerary.'},
 {q:'Can the group choose between several destination options?',a:'Yes. Early planning can compare two or three realistic destinations against the same criteria so the organizer can make a more informed choice.'},
 {q:'Can a custom trip become a repeatable annual program?',a:'Yes. Once a community understands its preferred trip style and traveler profile, later departures can often be developed more efficiently while still improving the itinerary.'}
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Custom Group Trip Planning | Talon Expeditions" description="Custom group trip planning for clubs, communities, businesses, studios, teams, friends, and organizer-led departures, with itinerary design and worldwide travel coordination." image={images.planning} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>
  <section class="av-inner-hero" style={`background-image:url('${images.planning}')`}><div class="shell"><h1>Custom Group Trip Planning</h1><Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs}/></div></section>
  <section class="av-detail-main"><div class="shell"><div class="av-detail-gallery"><div class="av-detail-gallery-main" style={`background-image:url('${images.planning}')`}></div><div class="av-detail-gallery-stack"><div style={`background-image:url('${images.train}')`}></div><div style={`background-image:url('${images.road}')`}></div></div></div><div class="av-detail-columns"><aside class="av-detail-sidebar"><div class="av-summary-card"><h3>Start From What You Know</h3><p>Custom planning can begin from the destination, the experience, or the group itself.</p><div class="av-summary-facts"><span>Destination already chosen</span><span>Experience already chosen</span><span>Group already formed</span><span>Dates still flexible</span><span>Worldwide planning</span></div></div><div class="av-day-card"><h3>Discovery</h3><p>Purpose, travelers, dates, source markets, activity, comfort, budget, and organizer priorities.</p></div><div class="av-day-card"><h3>Concept</h3><p>Destination options, trip style, duration, support model, and practical group-size assumptions.</p></div><div class="av-day-card"><h3>Design</h3><p>Route, lodging, transport, activities, local suppliers, free time, contingency, and commercial structure.</p></div></aside><article class="av-detail-content"><div class="answer-panel"><h2>What is custom group trip planning?</h2><p>Custom group trip planning means the itinerary and operating structure are developed around a specific group’s goals, dates, likely size, activity level, comfort, and budget rather than requiring the group to join a pre-designed departure.</p></div><h2>Start with the experience you want to create, then build the travel around it.</h2><p>Customization is most useful when the group has a reason for traveling together. A hiking club may want a particular route style. A dive community may need operator capacity and mixed certification options. A business team may want shared activities without a conference schedule. A social group may care most about private time, food, neighborhoods, and cultural experiences.</p><p>Those differences should change the trip. Custom planning gives us room to make those tradeoffs deliberately instead of hiding them behind a standard package name.</p><h3>Three common starting points</h3><div class="av-highlight-grid"><span>We know the destination</span><span>We know the experience</span><span>We know the group</span><span>We know the season</span><span>We have a rough budget</span><span>We only know what should feel different</span></div><section class="av-detail-section"><h2>Good customization is disciplined, not endless.</h2><p>Every change affects something else. More destinations increase transfers. More optionality may require additional transport or staffing. A lower target price may reduce private services. Higher activity can narrow the pool of travelers who can realistically join.</p><p>The earlier the trip is, the easier it is to change a bad assumption. That is why destination, duration, group size, activity, comfort, support, and approximate budget are tested before small details become expensive commitments.</p></section><section class="av-detail-section"><h2>Questions before we start designing</h2><FAQList items={faqs} openFirst={true}/></section></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="av-process"><div class="shell av-process-grid"><div class="av-process-visual" style={`background-image:url('${images.train}')`}><div class="av-process-callout"><h3>Decisions in the Right Order</h3><p>The earlier the trip is, the cheaper and easier it is to change a weak assumption.</p></div></div><div class="av-process-copy"><p class="eyebrow">The Planning Sequence</p><h2>From Broad Idea to Operational Itinerary</h2><p class="av-process-lead">We progressively reduce uncertainty, moving from purpose and fit into route design, supplier work, participant information, and final preparation.</p><div class="av-process-topline"><strong>Bring us the group, destination, or reason to go</strong><a href="/plan-a-trip/">↗</a></div><div class="av-process-steps"><div class="av-process-step"><div class="av-process-icon">◎</div><div><h3>Discover</h3><p>Clarify people, purpose, timing, expectations, and constraints.</p></div></div><div class="av-process-step"><div class="av-process-icon">⌖</div><div><h3>Compare</h3><p>Test destination and trip concepts against the same criteria.</p></div></div><div class="av-process-step"><div class="av-process-icon">▣</div><div><h3>Design</h3><p>Build the itinerary, supplier model, travel structure, and support.</p></div></div><div class="av-process-step"><div class="av-process-icon">▤</div><div><h3>Launch & Prepare</h3><p>Turn the plan into clear information, commitments, readiness, and departure coordination.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
